  SNYK-JS-PICOMATCH-21248802:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          picomatch@4.0.4 resolved via npm's own bundled tooling
          (npm@11.19.1 > node-gyp@12.4.0 > tinyglobby@0.2.17 > picomatch),
          surfaced only in the "lib" project (/usr/local/lib/node_modules);
          cica-web app scan clean. Build/CLI tooling only, never exercised
          by the running application. No upgrade or patch available.
          Recheck when a fix is published and npm bundles it.
        expires: '2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-BRACEEXPANSION-20244948:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          brace-expansion@5.0.9 resolved transitively via npm's bundled
          minimatch (npm@11.19.1 > minimatch@10.2.5 > brace-expansion@5.0.9).
          Build/CLI tooling only — not present in the application runtime
          path (cica-web app scan clean). Fixed in 5.0.11, but the version
          bundled by npm isn't independently controllable without patching
          npm's tree. Note: SNYK-JS-BRACEEXPANSION-18313044/18512280,
          previously ignored here, are confirmed resolved now that npm's
          bundled brace-expansion moved past those versions — removed from
          this file rather than left as dead entries. Recheck when npm
          bumps its bundled brace-expansion again.
        expires: '2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-BRACEEXPANSION-20244952:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Same root cause and dependency path as
          SNYK-JS-BRACEEXPANSION-20244948 — build/CLI tooling only, no
          direct upgrade available while bundled by npm (fixed in 5.0.10).
        expires: '2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-POSTCSSSELECTORPARSER-20510276:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          postcss-selector-parser@7.1.4 resolved transitively via npm's own
          dependency-resolution tooling (npm@11.19.1 > @npmcli/arborist@9.9.1
          > @npmcli/query@5.0.0 > postcss-selector-parser@7.1.4). Build/CLI
          tooling only, surfaced by the container scan against the "lib"
          project (/usr/local/lib/node_modules, npm's own global install) —
          not the application's own dependency tree (cica-web app scan
          clean). Fixed in postcss-selector-parser@7.1.6, but the version
          bundled by npm's own tree isn't independently controllable
          without patching npm itself. Recheck when npm bumps its bundled
          dependency.
        expires: '2026-11-09T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ATTR-17678182:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          libattr1, introduced by the base image
          node:24.18.1-trixie-slim via coreutils/adduser — a base-OS
          package, not an application dependency. No fix published for
          Debian 13 (trixie); base-image upgrade recommendations do not
          resolve it. Accepted pending upstream Debian patch or a base-image
          migration. Recheck on base-image bump.
        expires: '2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ACL-17677866:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          libacl1, introduced by the base image
          node:24.18.1-trixie-slim via coreutils/sed/adduser/dpkg — a
          base-OS package, not an application dependency. No fix published
          for Debian 13 (trixie); base-image upgrade recommendations do not
          resolve it. Accepted pending upstream Debian patch or a base-image
          migration. Recheck on base-image bump.
        expires: '2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-GCC14-20386241:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          libstdc++6, introduced by the base image node:24.18.1-trixie-slim
          via apt/gcc-14 — a base-OS package, not an application dependency.
          No fix published for Debian 13 (trixie); base-image upgrade
          recommendations do not resolve it. Accepted pending upstream
          Debian patch or a deliberate base-image migration. Recheck on
          base-image bump.
        expires: '2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-DEBIAN13-ZLIB-19520500:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          zlib1g, introduced by the base image node:24.18.1-trixie-slim via
          dpkg/apt — a base-OS package, not an application dependency. No
          fix published for Debian 13 (trixie) yet; base-image upgrade
          recommendations (e.g. alpine) are a separate, bigger migration and
          not being done as a point fix. Accepted pending upstream Debian
          patch or a deliberate base-image migration. Recheck on base-image
          bump.
        expires: '2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506894:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Both nanoid() call sites (CSP nonce in app.js, request-id fallback in the logger) call with no size argument on the secure export.
          The vulnerable functions (customAlphabet/customRandom and the
          nanoid/non-secure module) are never imported, and no user input
          reaches the size parameter, so the infinite-loop DoS is
          unreachable. Fix available in nanoid@5.1.16.
        expires: '2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506897:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Same root cause as SNYK-JS-NANOID-18506894 — no-arg nanoid() on the secure export, vulnerable paths not imported, DoS unreachable.
        expires: '2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-UPSTREAM-NODE-18507940:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          node-tar hardlink directory-traversal (CVE-2026-26960) bundled in
          the node:24.18.1-trixie-slim base image. Exploitable only by
          extracting an attacker-controlled tar archive; node-tar is present
          as a build-time/npm-install dependency, not invoked by the running
          cica-web application, which does not extract untrusted archives at
          runtime. Not bound to the network stack (requires local
          read/write/execute). Fixed upstream in Node 26.5.0. Recheck on
          base-image upgrade.
        expires: '2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-HTTPCACHESEMANTICS-19964064:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Origin validation flaw in http-cache-semantics' _varyMatches(),
          which can let a Vary:* response be reused across different
          users/requests sharing the same cache. Reachable only if got's
          built-in HTTP response caching (via cacheable-request) is actually
          enabled. Checked every got() call site in this app — the two in
          questionnaire/request-service.js and the one inside
          openid-client/lib/helpers/request.js — and none pass a `cache`
          option; openid-client's own caching (JWKS/throttling) uses a
          separate in-memory lru-cache, unrelated to got's HTTP cache. No fix
          available without an ESM migration: http-cache-semantics@4.3.0 is
          the latest version ever published (no patched release exists), and
          the only upgrade paths (got@12+, or express-openid-connect@3 for
          openid-client@6) are both ESM-only, which breaks this CommonJS
          codebase's require() calls — confirmed by reverting an attempted
          express-openid-connect@3 upgrade after it broke 86 tests with
          "Must use import to load ES Module". Tracked as a separate,
          deliberate future migration, not a point fix.
        expires: '2026-11-06T00:00:00.000Z'
  SNYK-JS-HTTPCACHESEMANTICS-19964068:
    - '*':
        reason: >
          Same root cause and same verified-unreachable basis as
          SNYK-JS-HTTPCACHESEMANTICS-19964064 — got's HTTP response caching
          is never enabled anywhere in this app's dependency chain, so the
          improper-authorisation variant of the same underlying bug is
          equally unreachable. See that entry for the full reasoning.
        expires: '2026-11-06T00:00:00.000Z'